== day_end_1998
  [card]
Everything she didn't do also happened.
  [pause 0.2]
Ruth spends the morning at the neighbour's, watching the door.
  [who Ruth]
The stocktake waits. The bank doesn't.
  [who "the shop"]
Tom looks for her in the stand until half-time.
  [who Tom]
Danny eats at the table alone and wraps her plate in foil.
  [who Danny]
The piano stays shut. It has been shut for thirteen years.
  [who herself]
== found_1998
  [card]
A week after the funeral she clears the till drawer at the shop. Under the float, an envelope, soft from being opened and folded and opened.
Royal College of Music, 1958: “…pleased to offer Mr F. Marlowe a place, beginning in the autumn term…”
  [quoted]
She already knew. It doesn't help.
  [pause 0.3]
[carried += gave]
== years
  [years]
Tom stops ringing on Sundays. Then starts again, years later, about nothing.
  [year 1999]
The bank takes the shop. She says it was the stocktake. It wasn't the stocktake.
  [year 2003]
Ruth moves to Toronto. She rings at odd hours and never says why.
  [year 2007]
She sells the piano to the primary school and goes once to hear the children. She leaves at the interval.
  [year 2016]
Danny starts eating earlier. She starts eating later. They meet in the middle at the sink.
  [year 2024]
She takes the lid off the piano at the school, once, at night. Then she puts it back.
  [year 2035]
Iris died on a Tuesday.
  [year 2039] [pause 1.2] [bold]
